[2026-04-05 15:16:10] Cross-checked the current SYSCTL public driver surface against the BOOTCFG and USER_REG families and reviewed adjacent driver patterns for API recommendations.
Files reviewed: TM4C129E_DriverLib/xDriver_MCU/SYSCTL/Driver/SYSCTL_Driver.h; TM4C129E_DriverLib/xDriver_MCU/SYSCTL/Driver/xHeader/SYSCTL_ResetVectorPointer.h; TM4C129E_DriverLib/xDriver_MCU/SYSCTL/Driver/xHeader/SYSCTL_NonVolatileMemoryInfo.h; TM4C129E_DriverLib/xDriver_MCU/SYSCTL/Driver/xHeader/SYSCTL_SystemProperties.h; TM4C129E_DriverLib/xDriver_MCU/SYSCTL/Driver/xHeader/SYSCTL_UniqueID.h; TM4C129E_DriverLib/xDriver_MCU/SYSCTL/Driver/xSource/SYSCTL_ResetVectorPointer.c; TM4C129E_DriverLib/xDriver_MCU/SYSCTL/Driver/xSource/SYSCTL_SystemProperties.c.
Findings: Existing public SYSCTL families are narrow and semantic. Single-field informational registers use one getter per register or per semantic bit, and current SYSCTL_Driver.h exports getter-style headers for reset-vector pointer, system properties, unique ID, and NVMSTAT. No public BOOTCFG or USER_REG family exists today.
Working recommendation direction: keep BOOTCFG read-side only if promoted at all, and keep any non-volatile commit/programming path in FLASH rather than SYSCTL. USER_REG may justify a narrowly scoped staged read/write family only if separated from commit semantics; otherwise keep it read-side only as well.
Status: awaiting final confirmation from FLASH-side search.
